hem put it out with less big name competitors, and therefore helps them secure more of a profit, and to fine tune and tweak the game even more. This is nothing but a good thing for Bloodlines fans.<br /> <br /> I know I wasn't going to be able to fine time to play Bloodlines with Cyberpunk and Persona 5 Royal, and FF7 Remake all being released in the same year... Now I know what I'm looking forward to for 2021.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is Cyberpunk 2077 so hyped? Isn\u2019t based on a obscure tabletop game,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T11:10:54-07:00","id":1407730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1407491-bloodlines-2-delayed-to-2021?p=1407727#post1407727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why is Cyberpunk 2077 so hyped? Isn\u2019t based on a obscure tabletop game,</div> </div> </div> </div>The same way the Witcher games were based on an obscure Polish fantasy series (which it was save in Poland where it was the Lord of the Rings-level popular). The Witcher 3 was one of the most popular games of all time and now everyone is hyped about them trying to do the same thing with a science fiction property.<br /> <br /> And Cyberpunk 2020 is about as obscure as &quot;Call of Cthulhu.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's VERY beloved in its circles.<br /> <br /> Especially if you know Shadow Run is just, &quot;Cyberpunk 2020 with Elves.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-12-2020, 02:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T11:18:35-07:00","id":1407732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1407491-bloodlines-2-delayed-to-2021?p=1407726#post1407726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its not a year also, since it's been delayed to first quarter 2021.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably subject to change depending on Halos revised release date","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T11:35:47-07:00","id":1407734,"title":"","content":"A smart move for Bloodlines 2 would be to use this opportunity to make more DLC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T11:43:43-07:00","id":1407735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1407491-bloodlines-2-delayed-to-2021?p=1407727#post1407727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why is Cyberpunk 2077 so hyped? Isn\u2019t based on a obscure tabletop game,</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Cyberpunk 2020 is not obscure in the tabletop community... As Phipps said, It's about as Obscure as Call of Cthulu, it's the father of all Cyberpunk games. Many people consider Shadowrun to be the deritivative less creative younger brother of 2020.<br /> <br /> CDprojekt Red is beloved by the serious Gamer community, they're one of the last developers out there which don't have excessive monitization processes. No microtransactions, no crappy DLC... and the Quality of the Witcher Games speak for themselves... Witcher 3 is rightly considered one of the very best games of the last Decade, easily in the top 10, and many people's number 1 (Dark Souls is my own number 1).<br /> <br /> The hype around Cyberpunk and the videos showing what you're going to be able to do in that game... the Freedom of choice in it... Hell, the main story can just end without you being involved, based on certain actions and descisions you make in the game...<br /> <br /> As for Bloodlines... It too is a Triple A game, it's got a full budget behind it, it's not meant to be small, it's meant to be a big grand release. Being pushed back is par for the course and a good thing, because it means they're tweaking things further, and tightening down on it. As Miyamoto, the father of Mario has said <span style=\"color:#121212\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">&quot;A delayed game is eventually good, but a rushed game is forever bad,&quot;</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T13:24:01-07:00","id":1407760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orphan81</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1407491-bloodlines-2-delayed-to-2021?p=1407735#post1407735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Cyberpunk 2020 is not obscure in the tabletop community... As Phipps said, It's about as Obscure as Call of Cthulu, it's the father of all Cyberpunk games. Many people consider Shadowrun to be the deritivative less creative younger brother of 2020.<br /> <br /> CDprojekt Red is beloved by the serious Gamer community, they're one of the last developers out there which don't have excessive monitization processes. No microtransactions, no crappy DLC... and the Quality of the Witcher Games speak for themselves... Witcher 3 is rightly considered one of the very best games of the last Decade, easily in the top 10, and many people's number 1 (Dark Souls is my own number 1).<br /> <br /> The hype around Cyberpunk and the videos showing what you're going to be able to do in that game... the Freedom of choice in it... Hell, the main story can just end without you being involved, based on certain actions and descisions you make in the game...<br /> <br /> As for Bloodlines... It too is a Triple A game, it's got a full budget behind it, it's not meant to be small, it's meant to be a big grand release. Being pushed back is par for the course and a good thing, because it means they're tweaking things further, and tightening down on it. As Miyamoto, the father of Mario has said <span style=\"color:#121212\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">&quot;A delayed game is eventually good, but a rushed game is forever bad,&quot;</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> oh god not another one that qoute's miyamoto. I have been reading in it every article i have seen today because halo infinite got delayed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Couldn't agree more about the points you made about cyberpunk but i don't believe bloodlines 2 is meant to be a triple a game. It's a small studio with a small budget. Let's hope they can deliver a good double a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T13:28:30-07:00","id":1407761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1407491-bloodlines-2-delayed-to-2021?p=1407726#post1407726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its not a year also, since it's been delayed to first quarter 2021.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Isn't the delay to 2021? Correct me if i am wrong but i dont believe they metionend a quarter","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T13:36:17-07:00","id":1407763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1407491-bloodlines-2-delayed-to-2021?p=1407727#post1407727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why is Cyberpunk 2077 so hyped? Isn\u2019t based on a obscure tabletop game,</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really about the franchise but about who is making the game. CDPR really could have picked any franchise or even a new ip as their next game and it still would have been the most anticipated game of the year. And to be fair the footage they have showed so far has been pretty impressive. Not mindblowing but enough to entice you to buy the game. The footage combined with the studio behind it and the things they have promised (which most people would believe cause they are CDPR) makes it the biggest game of the year.<br /> <br /> If only they were the ones that were making bloodlines 2 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","user":"blackshade","date":". 08-12-2020, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T13:44:33-07:00","id":1407767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orphan81</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1407491-bloodlines-2-delayed-to-2021?p=1407735#post1407735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Cyberpunk 2020 is not obscure in the tabletop community... As Phipps said, It's about as Obscure as Call of Cthulu, it's the father of all Cyberpunk games. Many people consider Shadowrun to be the deritivative less creative younger brother of 2020.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know who those people are, but they couldn't possibly be further from the truth. Cyberpunk 2020 has managed to leave virtually none of its DNA in tabletop gaming. Neither its mechanics nor its setting led to any innovations.<br /> <br /> Shadowrun, at the bare minimum, popularized dicepools, which majorly influenced the development of Vampire the Masquerade. I'm also not sure what relation you can draw between Shadowrun and Cyberpunk2020 that wouldn't be just genre conventions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T13:47:36-07:00","id":1407770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1407491-bloodlines-2-delayed-to-2021#post1407491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.vg247.com/2020/08/11/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-2021-delay/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.vg247.com/2020/08/11/vam...-2-2021-delay/</a><br /> Bad sign. Development must be a mess. We do not even know if It will be out in Q1,Q2 or Q3.</div> </div> </div> </div>10/08/2020:<br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/mKaau7Y.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> 11/08/2020:<br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/EV5zkoZ.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Red flags all around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T14:01:14-07:00","id":1407773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1407491-bloodlines-2-delayed-to-2021?p=1407767#post1407767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know who those people are, but they couldn't possibly be further from the truth. Cyberpunk 2020 has managed to leave virtually none of its DNA in tabletop gaming. Neither its mechanics nor its setting led to any innovations.<br /> <br /> Shadowrun, at the bare minimum, popularized dicepools, which majorly influenced the development of Vampire the Masquerade. I'm also not sure what relation you can draw between Shadowrun and Cyberpunk2020 that wouldn't be just genre conventions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Cyberpunk 2020 DEFINED those genre conventions. Runners, losing bits of yourself as you by more cyberware in an objective essence/psychosis fashion. Much like the very idea of vampires having elaborate secret societies with rulers by city and specific bloodlines with unique powers can be laid entirely at the feet of Masquerade. Much of what we consider &quot;Base&quot; urban fantasy or horror was first defined in masquerade.<br /> <br /> If you have cyberpunk in your game it probably takes ideas that were first defined in cyberpunk 2020. If you have it in your fiction it probably has ideas first defined in cyberpunk 2020.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T14:13:02-07:00","id":1407778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1407491-bloodlines-2-delayed-to-2021?p=1407773#post1407773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cyberpunk 2020 DEFINED those genre conventions.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://external-content.duckduckgo.com/iu/?u=https%3A%2F%2Ftse1.mm.bing.net%2Fth%3Fid%3DOIP.wQcx_R_38clp_586VY2ALQDQEr%26pid%3DApi&amp;f=1\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Though for posterity it must be noted that the order of releases is Cyberpunk 2013 (1988), Shadowrun 1E (1989), Cyberpunk 2020 (1990). So they are more of parallel evolutions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Much like the very idea of vampires having elaborate secret societies with rulers by city and specific bloodlines with unique powers can be laid entirely at the feet of Masquerade. Much of what we consider &quot;Base&quot; urban fantasy or horror was first defined in masquerade. </div> </div> </div>Interview With A Vampire, <i><b>Shadowrun</b></i>, and, crucially for urban fantasy, Bordertown, all predate Vampire the Masquerade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12892,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","user":"Kammerer","date":". 08-12-2020, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T14:20:37-07:00","id":1407780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1407491-bloodlines-2-delayed-to-2021#post1407491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.vg247.com/2020/08/11/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-2021-delay/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.vg247.com/2020/08/11/vam...-2-2021-delay/</a><br /> Bad sign. Development must be a mess. We do not even know if It will be out in Q1,Q2 or Q3.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The world is a mess right now. I'm sure development is chugging along fine, but these times are difficult for everyone. If they need a little more time to get the product out, we can wait. Paradox has been putting out good stuff for a long time, plus the early looks seem great, so I'm not worried.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T14:21:05-07:00","id":1407781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1407491-bloodlines-2-delayed-to-2021?p=1407767#post1407767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know who those people are, but they couldn't possibly be further from the truth. Cyberpunk 2020 has managed to leave virtually none of its DNA in tabletop gaming. Neither its mechanics nor its setting led to any innovations.<br /> <br /> Shadowrun, at the bare minimum, popularized dicepools, which majorly influenced the development of Vampire the Masquerade. I'm also not sure what relation you can draw between Shadowrun and Cyberpunk2020 that wouldn't be just genre conventions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Guess you're just going to ignore the massive influence Mike Pondsmith, one of the first people of Color in RPGs, the creator of Cyberpunk 2020 has had over the entire industry, how Cyberpunk influenced freaking VAMPIRE THE MASQUERADE ITSELF so much so they actually had a cross-over... But yeah man, you keep saying blatant lies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T14:28:19-07:00","id":1407782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1407491-bloodlines-2-delayed-to-2021?p=1407763#post1407763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not really about the franchise but about who is making the game. CDPR really could have picked any franchise or even a new ip as their next game and it still would have been the most anticipated game of the year. And to be fair the footage they have showed so far has been pretty impressive. Not mindblowing but enough to entice you to buy the game. The footage combined with the studio behind it and the things they have promised (which most people would believe cause they are CDPR) makes it the biggest game of the year.<br /> <br /> If only they were the ones that were making bloodlines 2 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Cyberpunk 2077 has been in development for about 8 years. We should be glad Bloodlines 2 is having a much more reasonable schedule.<br /> <br /> Re: Mike Pondsmith<br /> <br /> Mike Pondsmith is very open about the fact that the developers of White Wolf have been a bit cagey about that he created CP2020 as a blender of all the things that he loved and put them in a blender: Neuromancer [later installed], Bubblegum Crisis, Max Headroom [which was good, honest!], Mad Max, Hardwired, Akira, and so on.<br /> <br /> What Mike managed to achieve was create a living world around all these various cyberpunk concepts with answering questions about, &quot;How do megacorps function in a divided United States of America?&quot; Creating the concepts of a bunch of mercenaries doing jobs for corporations as a regular thing (versus the one-off job in Neuromancer) and so on.<br /> <br /> It's sort of like &quot;Cthulhu existed before Call of Cthulhu but the concepts of a bunch of 1920s investigators fighting cults, while having some origins in HPL's work, was mostly made by the people at Chaosium--particularly with the idea of all the various monsters existing in one world.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-12-2020, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T14:29:40-07:00","id":1407784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orphan81</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1407491-bloodlines-2-delayed-to-2021?p=1407781#post1407781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guess you're just going to ignore the massive influence Mike Pondsmith, one of the first people of Color in RPGs, the creator of Cyberpunk 2020 has had over the entire industry</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be the influence of Mike Pondsmith, not of the game he made.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> how Cyberpunk influenced freaking VAMPIRE THE MASQUERADE ITSELF so much so they actually had a cross-over... But yeah man, you keep saying blatant lies. </div> </div> </div>Do you mean the articles in <i>White Wolf Magazine</i> #36, 37, &amp; 38, or &quot;Night's Edge&quot;, a third party brand scrubbed hack for Cyberpunk 2020? Either way, that's not a sign of the lasting legacy of Cyberpunk 2020 in tabletop RPGs. I wasn't saying &quot;Cyberpunk2020 is an unknown game no one ever cared for&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T14:33:47-07:00","id":1407786,"title":"","content":"Seriously, the idea of Cyberpunk 2020 not being influential is....silly.<br /> <br /> It was a massively influential game.<br /> <br /> But I admit you might not know this if you didn't read books like this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Designers-Dragons-History-Roleplaying-Industry-ebook/dp/B00R8RARVA/ref=sr_1_2?dchild=1&amp;keywords=Eighties+Roleplaying+Games&amp;qid=1597267529&amp;sr=8-2\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Designers-Dragons-History-Roleplaying-Industry-ebook/dp/B00R8RARVA/ref=sr_1_2?dchild=1&amp;keywords=Eighties+Roleplaying+Games&amp;qid=1597267529&amp;sr=8-2\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Designers-Dragons-History-Roleplaying-Industry-ebook/dp/B00R8RARVA/ref=sr_1_2?dchild=1&amp;keywords=Eighties+Roleplaying+Games&amp;qid=1597267529&amp;sr=8-2\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.amazon.com/Designers-Dragons-History-Roleplaying-Industry-ebook/dp/B00R8RARVA/ref=sr_1_2?dchild=1&amp;keywords=Eighties+Roleplaying+Games&amp;qid=1597267529&amp;sr=8-2 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-12-2020, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T14:35:06-07:00","id":1407787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1407491-bloodlines-2-delayed-to-2021?p=1407782#post1407782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Creating the concepts of a bunch of mercenaries doing jobs for corporations as a regular thing (versus the one-off job in Neuromancer)</div> </div> </div> </div>Turner, one of the protagonists of Count Zero, is a professional unaffiliated corporate mercenary doing jobs for corporations as a regular thing. And if you look for it, you can see the legs of Solo, Techie, Med-Techie, Corpo and Netrunner roles in the team he's working with. Turner's also the source for Shadowrun's Edge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T14:37:26-07:00","id":1407789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1407491-bloodlines-2-delayed-to-2021?p=1407787#post1407787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Turner, one of the protagonists of Count Zero, is a professional unaffiliated corporate mercenary doing jobs for corporations as a regular thing. And if you look for it, you can see the legs of Solo, Techie, Med-Techie, Corpo and Netrunner roles in the team he's working with. Turner's also the source for Shadowrun's Edge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep and it was Mike who popularized it among gamers, not Count Zero.<br /> <br /> And before you dismiss this claim, allow me to illustrate.<br /> <br /> &quot;What game would you be doing this in?&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is to say that you needed a cyberpunk game to do it and....Mike was the guy who published it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T14:37:48-07:00","id":1407790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1407491-bloodlines-2-delayed-to-2021?p=1407784#post1407784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be the influence of Mike Pondsmith, not of the game he made.<br /> <br /> Do you mean the articles in <i>White Wolf Magazine</i> #36, 37, &amp; 38, or &quot;Night's Edge&quot;, a third party brand scrubbed hack for Cyberpunk 2020? Either way, that's not a sign of the lasting legacy of Cyberpunk 2020 in tabletop RPGs. I wasn't saying &quot;Cyberpunk2020 is an unknown game no one ever cared for&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's exactly what you're saying, and you've been proven wrong, but you're to proud to admit it. Cyberpunk 2020 is considered one of the seminal RPGS that's influenced generations after it. But hey man, you focus on that need to be &quot;right&quot; and discount it all... I guess all that Hype around Cyberpunk 2077 is all fake too right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T14:46:00-07:00","id":1407794,"title":"","content":"Putting this in the right topic now!<br /> <br /> Let's be clear here... Cyberpunk 2020 had so much influence, a damn Eastern European Video game company, whose first language isn't even English, decided to buy the rights to it, Lock, Stock, and Barrel... and Bring it's creator on board to help them create the story.<br /> <br /> They have enough &quot;Fuck you&quot; money they could have gotten William Gibson if they wanted to. They didn't want to create Nueromancer the Videogame, or Count Zero, Or All Tomorrow's Parties, or Burning Chrome the video game..<br /> <br /> They wanted to make CYBERPUNK the Videogame. They wanted Mike Pondsmith, not William Gibson.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T14:46:36-07:00","id":1407797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orphan81</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1407491-bloodlines-2-delayed-to-2021?p=1407790#post1407790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's exactly what you're saying, and you've been proven wrong, but you're to proud to admit it. Cyberpunk 2020 is considered one of the seminal RPGS that's influenced generations after it. But hey man, you focus on that need to be &quot;right&quot; and discount it all... I guess all that Hype around Cyberpunk 2077 is all fake too right?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Let's all just tone it down a bit.</span><br /> <br /> HOWEVER, I should point out even Mike Pondsmith was a bit confused when CD_Projket Red contacted him.<br /> <br /> He had no idea he was huge in Poland.<br /> <br /> Because it had become a massive underground gaming scene via piracy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/HDVu4l8j-kI\" data-code=\"HDVu4l8j-kI\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/HDVu4l8j-kI/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 08-12-2020, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T15:46:35-07:00","id":1407804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1407491-bloodlines-2-delayed-to-2021?p=1407778#post1407778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"https://external-content.duckduckgo.com/iu/?u=https%3A%2F%2Ftse1.mm.bing.net%2Fth%3Fid%3DOIP.wQcx_R_38clp_586VY2ALQDQEr%26pid%3DApi&amp;f=1\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Though for posterity it must be noted that the order of releases is Cyberpunk 2013 (1988), Shadowrun 1E (1989), Cyberpunk 2020 (1990). So they are more of parallel evolutions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not really, its like saying all fantasy is a direct port from Lord of the Rings. When much or our idea of fantasy archtypes are were more or less codfied by D&amp;D. Cyberpunk 2020 codified what we think of as cyberpunk as a playable genre. Are there clear takes from other media? absolutely but the whole tone and system you generally have for anything resembling cyberpunk media comes through the codfication that is 2020.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Interview With A Vampire, <i><b>Shadowrun</b></i>, and, crucially for urban fantasy, Bordertown, all predate Vampire the Masquerade. </div> </div> </div>Have you read any of those? The idea of vampire clans, a camarilla alike.. etc the idea that vampire generally are at war with werewolves. These are all so codified in modern vampire stories that peo0ple who have no familiarity with Masquerade consider them baseline. Compare Twilight and Interview with a Vampire. YOu can see which one takes VTM tropes as &quot;a baseline&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T05:51:42-07:00","id":1407907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orphan81</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1407491-bloodlines-2-delayed-to-2021?p=1407735#post1407735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Cyberpunk 2020 is not obscure in the tabletop community... As Phipps said, It's about as Obscure as Call of Cthulu, it's the father of all Cyberpunk games. Many people consider Shadowrun to be the deritivative less creative younger brother of 2020.<br /> <br /> CDprojekt Red is beloved by the serious Gamer community, they're one of the last developers out there which don't have excessive monitization processes. No microtransactions, no crappy DLC... and the Quality of the Witcher Games speak for themselves... Witcher 3 is rightly considered one of the very best games of the last Decade, easily in the top 10, and many people's number 1 (Dark Souls is my own number 1).<br /> <br /> The hype around Cyberpunk and the videos showing what you're going to be able to do in that game... the Freedom of choice in it... Hell, the main story can just end without you being involved, based on certain actions and descisions you make in the game...<br /> <br /> As for Bloodlines... It too is a Triple A game, it's got a full budget behind it, it's not meant to be small, it's meant to be a big grand release. Being pushed back is par for the course and a good thing, because it means they're tweaking things further, and tightening down on it. As Miyamoto, the father of Mario has said <span style=\"color:#121212\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">&amp;quot;A delayed game is eventually good, but a rushed game is forever bad,&amp;quot;</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve never liked Cyberpunk, it\u2019s to close to reality to be fun, like old Cyberpunk stories have just been only slightly more shot from reality thanks to various governments Love Affair with Neoliberalism.<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t hear about Huge corporations owning everything and companies treating the environment like a trash can. Because that\u2019s just reality l<br /> plus it\u2019s probably not a part of Cyberpunk 2077.<br /> <br /> But a lot of cyberpunk series doesn\u2019t do anything with the whole mega corps owning everyone and trees are rarer then robots thing isn\u2019t used for political commentary, they just use it as a setting. With the characters not really caring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T09:31:58-07:00","id":1407961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1407491-bloodlines-2-delayed-to-2021?p=1407907#post1407907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019ve never liked Cyberpunk, it\u2019s to close to reality to be fun, like old Cyberpunk stories have just been only slightly more shot from reality thanks to various governments Love Affair with Neoliberalism.<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t hear about Huge corporations owning everything and companies treating the environment like a trash can. Because that\u2019s just reality l<br /> plus it\u2019s probably not a part of Cyberpunk 2077.<br /> <br /> But a lot of cyberpunk series doesn\u2019t do anything with the whole mega corps owning everyone and trees are rarer then robots thing isn\u2019t used for political commentary, they just use it as a setting. With the characters not really caring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cyberpunk is a subset of noir for the most part which is French for &quot;black.&quot; The idea of noir fiction in detective stories and mysteries is that the system is utterly rotten. The police can't be trusted, the super-rich are untouchable, and so on. Which is to say that cyberpunk reflects reality but also detective fiction of the 1930s and 1940s was also the exact same way the world is today.<br /> <br /> Mike Pondsmith has stated that the Edgerunners of Cyberpunk 2013/2020/2077 aren't actually supposed to be apathetic to the plight of the common man. That fighting the corporations is something that you're supposed to do and bring them down. The Rockerboy, The Newspaper reporter, and others are characters designed to legitimately fight the system.<br /> <br /> However, equally valid is meant to be the &quot;Jerk with a Heart of Gold&quot; storyline where you don't fight the system but just try and do what little good you can. These are the bread and butter of the Witcher storylines and what CDPR excells at.<br /> <br /> Basically, a megacorp boss wants to get his mistress back and brainwashed? You can rescue her, get her a new life, and maybe get the corporation to kill the megacorp boss for embarassing the company. Absolutely nothing has changed in the world but you've done your little part. SIN CITY-esque stories where the world is still a shithole but there's a few less bastards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T09:45:19-07:00","id":1407967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.bloodlines2.com/en/production-in-the-age-of-covid-19\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http:https://orebtvnsretjvneokqmefoiunm.s3.amazonaws.com/uploads/img/65prc/production-schedule-b9d2ec.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.bloodlines2.com/en/production-in-the-age-of-covid-19\" target=\"_blank\"> Production in the age of COVID-19 | VtM: Bloodlines 2 </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.bloodlines2.com/en/production-in-the-age-of-covid-19\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.bloodlines2.com/en/production-in-the-age-of-covid-19 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Austin Maestre chats a little bit on how COVID-19 has changed things up for producers. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The devs posted a blog post on how COVID-19 is affecting development.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Storyteller of Boston by Night on Twitch <a href=\"https://www.twitch.tv/theonyxpath\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.twitch.tv/theonyxpath</a><br /> Fan of WOD Since 2013","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26354-michelleclight","name":"MichelleCLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26354_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T10:18:37-07:00","id":1407974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1407491-bloodlines-2-delayed-to-2021?p=1407907#post1407907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019ve never liked Cyberpunk, it\u2019s to close to reality to be fun, like old Cyberpunk stories have just been only slightly more shot from reality thanks to various governments Love Affair with Neoliberalism.<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t hear about Huge corporations owning everything and companies treating the environment like a trash can. Because that\u2019s just reality l<br /> plus it\u2019s probably not a part of Cyberpunk 2077.<br /> <br /> But a lot of cyberpunk series doesn\u2019t do anything with the whole mega corps owning everyone and trees are rarer then robots thing isn\u2019t used for political commentary, they just use it as a setting. With the characters not really caring.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hear you. I can't watch Silicon Valley because it's too close to what I do and we already made all those jokes a long time ago (I don't actually live there, but work in tech). I had my cyber punk &quot;We are living in the future&quot; moment over a decade ago when I saw a bunch homeless people clustered around a laptop and realized I was in a less polluted version of Max Headroom. But there's still a fantasy element to these games and the genre. I don't get to have shoot outs, cybernetic implants and rip people off in real life. I could care less about the Witcher, only played the first 2 and Geralt was boring as hell, but the setting for Cyberpunk looks a lot more interesting with more choice and decision and consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T10:49:35-07:00","id":1407984,"title":"","content":"not unexpected, nothing to worry about imho,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T16:17:02-07:00","id":1408063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1407491-bloodlines-2-delayed-to-2021?p=1407907#post1407907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019ve never liked Cyberpunk, it\u2019s to close to reality to be fun, like old Cyberpunk stories have just been only slightly more shot from reality thanks to various governments Love Affair with Neoliberalism.<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t hear about Huge corporations owning everything and companies treating the environment like a trash can. Because that\u2019s just reality l<br /> plus it\u2019s probably not a part of Cyberpunk 2077.<br /> <br /> But a lot of cyberpunk series doesn\u2019t do anything with the whole mega corps owning everyone and trees are rarer then robots thing isn\u2019t used for political commentary, they just use it as a setting. With the characters not really caring.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the mistake we made was that governments were going to go away vs become an active participant and supporter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T16:36:56-07:00","id":1408069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1407491-bloodlines-2-delayed-to-2021?p=1408063#post1408063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the mistake we made was that governments were going to go away vs become an active participant and supporter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Governments haven't gone away in Cyberpunk 2020/2077's world. That's one of the things I like about it. The United States did break up, though with California being its own country now.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.redd.it/4uwrqwmlh4e41.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T08:34:49-07:00","id":1409141,"title":"","content":"Well in other news the Narrative lead has been fired and a creative director has quit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.rockpapershotgun.com/2020/08/19/brian-mitsoda-has-been-fired-as-narrative-lead-on-bloodlines-2/amp/?__twitter_impression=true\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/bloodlines-2-damsel.jpg?width=1200&amp;height=630&amp;fit=crop&amp;enable=upscale&amp;auto=webp\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.rockpapershotgun.com/2020/08/19/brian-mitsoda-has-been-fired-as-narrative-lead-on-bloodlines-2/amp/?__twitter_impression=true\" target=\"_blank\"> Brian Mitsoda has been fired as narrative lead on Bloodlines 2 </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.rockpapershotgun.com/2020/08/19/brian-mitsoda-has-been-fired-as-narrative-lead-on-bloodlines-2/amp/?__twitter_impression=true\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.rockpapershotgun.com/2020/08/19/brian-mitsoda-has-been-fired-as-narrative-lead-on-bloodlines-2/amp/?__twitter_impression=true </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Brian Mitsoda has been \"suddenly terminated\" from his position as narrative lead on Vampire: The Masquerade - Bloodlines 2. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T08:47:23-07:00","id":1409143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1407491-bloodlines-2-delayed-to-2021?p=1409141#post1409141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well in other news the Narrative lead has been fired and a 